  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
       5 · CUSTOMER OBJECTIONS
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="ll-sec ll-sec-alt" id="objections">
    <div class="ll-narrow">
      <div class="ll-sec-head center">
        <span class="ll-kicker">Honest Answers</span>
        <h2>Questions Cat Owners Are Already Asking</h2>
        <p class="ll-lede">Read these before buying. Transparency helps you make the right decision.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ll-obj-grid">

        <div class="ll-obj open">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Does it handle urine and wet clumps?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            LitterLoops™ is designed for use with clumping litter. When your cat urinates, the moisture is absorbed and forms a solid clump. When you rotate the drum, the internal sieve catches these solid clumps and directs them into the waste drawer, while loose, unsoiled granules filter back through. For best results, allow a few minutes after your cat uses the box before rotating.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Will litter stick to the bottom?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            Maintaining the correct litter depth (as shown in the included instructions) helps prevent clumps from forming directly against the basin floor. If litter depth is insufficient or if a cat urinates directly against the side wall, some manual loosening may occasionally be required. The smooth interior surface is designed to minimize sticking, but some maintenance is normal.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Does it control odor?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            LitterLoops™ uses an open design that cats feel comfortable entering. The collection drawer helps contain separated waste. However, because the design is open, it does not seal odors the way an enclosed automatic box might. Regular rotation and prompt waste removal are your primary tools for managing odor. Using an odor-control clumping litter will also help.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Will it work for larger cats?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            Please check the product specifications on your order confirmation or in the included instructions for the confirmed size and weight recommendations. If your cat is a large breed such as a Maine Coon or Ragdoll, we recommend reviewing the listed dimensions before purchase to confirm it is a suitable fit.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Will my cat feel stable while using it?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            The drum sits in a fixed cradle base. It does not rotate on its own — only when you manually turn it. When your cat is inside using the box, the unit remains stationary. The base is designed to stay in place during normal use.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>What types of litter can I use?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            LitterLoops™ requires a clumping litter to work correctly. The sifting mechanism relies on solid clumps forming so they can be retained by the sieve. Non-clumping litters, large wood pellets, paper pellets, or non-clumping crystals will not work with the separation mechanism. Please check the product specifications for the confirmed list of compatible litter types.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>How often do I need to empty the waste compartment?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            The frequency depends on how many cats use the box and how often they go. As a general guide, rotating daily and emptying the waste drawer every few days will keep the unit operating cleanly. The included instructions provide guidance specific to this unit.
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ll-obj">
          <div class="ll-obj-q">
            <span>Do I still need to do any manual cleaning?</span>
            <div class="ll-obj-icon">
              <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ll-obj-a">
            Yes. LitterLoops™ significantly simplifies daily waste removal, but it does not eliminate all cleaning. Periodic basin rinse-downs and occasional spot cleaning will still be necessary, as with any litter box. It is an easier routine — not a hands-free one.
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
